2. Natural Earth
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source:
  Natural Earth, 1:50m Admin 0 - Countries (ne_50m_admin_0_countries),
  https://www.naturalearthdata.com/ (nvkelso/natural-earth-vector).

Natural Earth data are in the public domain.

Affected files in this repository:
  scripts/data/brazil_ne50m_mainland.json   (exterior ring of mainland Brazil)
  scripts/data/setores_zida_27.json         (border geometry derived from it)
  configs/zida_shield_default.yaml          (border coordinates derived from it)
  configs/border_sectors.yaml               (border coordinates derived from it)

The border geometry is a generalized, world-scale cartographic representation
used to generate simulated incursions. It is not a legal boundary demarcation.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Miranda (2025) - methodological reference
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The incursion-generation method (border sectors, normal sector distribution,
inward heading with Gaussian deviation) is adapted from Miranda (2025), ITA
thesis. No data from that work is redistributed: the 27 sectors, their
numbering and their cumulative distribution are this project's own
construction.

